SUMMARY:Bluegrass and Ice Cream
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\nGathering on the third Sunday evening each 
 month in the Hendersonville Presbyterian Church (HPC) community room\, a c
 rowd of up to 200 people enjoy a special blend of bluegrass and gospel mus
 ic interspersed with humorous anecdotes and inspirational messages — and
  free ice cream and cookies to boot!\n\nUsually fewer than 20 percent of t
 hose attending are members of HPC. The rest of the audience comes from var
 ious backgrounds\, denominations and ages to hear the combination of origi
 nal gospel music and old-time Southern gospel songs. A love offering for t
 he band is taken\, but giving is strictly voluntary.\nHPC is located at th
 e corner of Seventh Avenue and Grove Street. Parking is in the rear of the
  church and accessible from Grove and King Streets and from Sixth Avenue. 
 For more information about the\nchurch and the Bash\, visit hendersonville
 pc.org or call the church office\, 828-692-3211.
